Overview

The AI Job Assistant is a Python-based system that builds an end-to-end AI recruitment pipeline. It automates job collection, stores structured data, and uses AI + deterministic scoring logic to evaluate job fit against a resume.

The system now operates as a multi-layer AI + rules-based matching engine, not just a simple scoring script.

🧠 Key Features
📡 Job Scraper
Scrapes job listings from Job Bank (Canada)
Extracts:
Job title
Company
Location
Job URL
Description (basic level, with future upgrade planned for deep scraping)
Generates unique job IDs using hashing
Stores jobs in SQLite database
🗄️ Database System (SQLite)
Fully migrated from CSV → relational database
Structured schema includes:
Job metadata:
title
company
location
url
description
Processing state:
status (new, analyzed)
AI output fields:
score (final computed score)
strengths
gaps
recommendation
Duplicate prevention using INSERT OR IGNORE
Enhanced row handling using sqlite3.Row for dictionary-style access
🤖 AI Extraction Engine (Improved Architecture)

The system no longer relies on AI for scoring.

Instead, GPT now acts as a structured information extractor.

It outputs:

{
  "required_skills": {
    "job_skills": [],
    "matched": [],
    "missing": []
  },
  "experience": {
    "required": "",
    "candidate": "",
    "match": ""
  },
  "responsibilities": {
    "matched": [],
    "missing": []
  },
  "education": {
    "matched": [],
    "missing": []
  },
  "strengths": [],
  "gaps": []
}

✔ AI = extraction only
✔ No scoring decisions made by AI

📊 Weighted Scoring Engine (NEW)

A deterministic Python scoring layer now calculates final job fit:

Skills match (40 pts)
Experience match (25 pts)
Responsibilities match (20 pts)
Education match (10 pts)
Output:
Final score (0–100)
Breakdown per category
Recommendation logic:
70+   → apply  
45–69 → maybe  
<45   → skip
